      "tile_id": "tile_stakeholder_tailoring_anticipating",
      "title": "Tailoring Detail and Anticipating Questions",
      "summary": "Learn to adjust information density and presentation order for technical vs. executive audiences, and to anticipate stakeholder questions by answering them in the writing.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "step_id": "tile_stakeholder_tailoring_anticipating.s01",
          "type": "explainer",
          "concept_ids": [
            "stakeholder.tailoring_detail_to_audience"
          ],
          "eyebrow": "Tailoring Detail",
          "title": "Same Finding, Different Audiences",
          "lede": "The Lagos delivery-time analysis might go to the operations manager or to the executive team. Both need the finding \u2014 but not the same amount of detail.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "text": "Designing with a specific person in mind helps avoid the 'mixed audience' trap. Knowing the audience's motivations lets you frame what they need to know or do in terms of those motivating factors. That knowledge should inform choices such as how much information density to include, and whether to add more context or explain something in greater detail.",
              "role": "mechanism",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.tailoring_detail_to_audience"
                ],
                "fact_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.tailoring_detail_to_audience#f1",
                  "stakeholder.tailoring_detail_to_audience#f2"
                ],
                "teaching_block_ids": [
                  "stakeholder.tailoring_detail_to_audience#tb1",
                  "stakeholder.tailoring_detail_to_audience#tb2"
                ]
              }
            },
