          ],
          "eyebrow": "Let's Revisit",
          "title": "Detail Order: Two Audiences, Two Approaches",
          "lede": "Compare how the same Lagos finding reads differently depending on who it is written for.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "text": "The operations manager wants to understand the analysis before hearing the recommendation \u2014 so the detail-first version opens with context (delivery times rose from 22 to 30 min), walks through the method, and ends with the ask. The executive wants the recommendation first and the high-level arc only \u2014 so the recommendation-first version leads with 'add one courier' and follows with the key finding. The structural difference is the signal: where the recommendation appears tells you which audience the version is written for.",
